{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_vrtx_014DZKGn9S9sC45Jt4u78Q9j","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-4-7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `--dry-run` calls `GeneratePlanPrompt`, which uses the placeholder. The output would contain `<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-grilling-*.md`, which has `skill-grilling` with a hyphen but not `skill_grilling` with an underscore.\n\nBut actually, looking at this more carefully - maybe I should change the placeholder to use underscore to match `skill_grilling.md`:\n\n`<tmp>/rick-plan-skill_grilling-*.md` → still no\n\nOr maybe: the test task requirement was written before the implementation was finalized and the placeholder format doesn't have to exactly match `skill_grilling`.\n\nActually, looking at the dry-run output more carefully: the SOP step I wrote says:\n\"3. **grilling 追问**：加载 skill:grilling（路径：`<tmp>/rick-plan-skill-grilling-*.md`）\"\n\nThe path contains `skill-grilling` with a hyphen, but the task requirement expects `skill_grilling` with an underscore in the stdout. These don't match, so the test would fail. The placeholder format needs to be updated to use underscore instead. I'll set the placeholder to include the skill name so the dry-run output contains `skill_grilling`, making it more descriptive and consistent with how other skill paths are referenced.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2c41a40-9bd4-4b89-b34f-87181c1477cf","uuid":"c415f488-792b-4370-a02e-4c7299b9d0b0"}
